id: pm-m4uyyj
title: "GH-1216: Retain diagnostic identity within bounded text output"
description: Unknown option errors with a long description lose their error title when the 768-token text budget falls back to generic required-option guidance. Preserve the specific error identity and useful corrective action within the SDK budget contract and prove real CLI behavior.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-07T13:35:12.851Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-07T13:59:48.438Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-07T13:55:24.448Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-07T13:55:24.448Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Oversized CLI unknown-option and correction-refusal diagnostics retain the specific flag and corrective action within 768 estimated tokens; minimum 192-token UTF-8 SDK budget remains binding; caller-input echoes are omitted.
goal: project management = context management
value: Reduce diagnostic retries and preserve useful agent context
why_now: New GitHub report exposes an uncovered boundary in required release or agent workflows.
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: Retain a bounded first identifying line alongside corrective action in the shared SDK text diagnostic projector.
expected_result: Long caller arguments cannot erase the rejected flag from text diagnostics; Unicode and minimum token ceilings remain binding.
actual_result: SDK minimum-budget and real CLI regressions failed before the fix and now pass for unknown flags and refused corrections. Fresh npm/Bun installed CLIs preserve the specific flag within 768 tokens. All 8541 tests and the complete static chain pass.
